     'Jawai sits roughly halfway between Udaipur and Jodhpur, which makes it a natural, low-stress stop on a Rajasthan tour.',
     [['Why it fits so well', 'You travel one way, from Udaipur through Jawai to Jodhpur, so there is no backtracking. Two nights in Bera break up palace-heavy itineraries with a different pace, open landscape and wildlife.'],
      ['A 7-day sample', '- Days 1–2: Udaipur. || - Days 3–4: Jawai (two nights, three drives) with Ranakpur on the way. || - Days 5–6: Jodhpur. || - Day 7: onward to Jaisalmer or fly out.'],
      ['A 10-day sample', 'Add Kumbhalgarh, a night near Jaisalmer, and Pushkar or Jaipur at one end. Keep Jawai as a slow pause in the middle so you are not rushing everything.'],
      ['Tips', 'Book Jawai’s drives early for winter, give yourself at least two nights, and avoid arriving after dark. See [Rajasthan Jawai Udaipur road trip](blog/udaipur-jawai-ranakpur-kumbhalgarh-road-trip-plan).']],
     [['How many nights should I give Jawai in a Rajasthan tour?', 'Two nights at least, three if wildlife is a priority.'],
      ['Is Jawai worth it compared with more forts?', 'It offers something different: wild landscapes and leopards, and a break from crowds. Many guests call it the highlight.'],
      ['Which direction is best?', 'Udaipur to Jawai to Jodhpur is the most popular, but the reverse works equally well.']], 'plan'],

    ['extend-golden-triangle-tour-with-jawai', 'Extending a Golden Triangle Tour with Jawai', 'Itinerary', '',
     'Delhi, Agra and Jaipur are well known. Here is how to add a wildlife leg in southern Rajasthan.',
     'Extend Your Golden Triangle Tour with a Jawai Leopard Safari',
     'How to add Jawai to a Delhi Agra Jaipur Golden Triangle tour: routes, flights, nights needed and sample extensions with Udaipur.',
     'Golden Triangle with Jawai, Jawai after Jaipur, Golden Triangle leopard safari, Delhi Agra Jaipur Jawai extension, Jawai Udaipur extension',
     'The Golden Triangle covers history. Adding Jawai gives you the other side of Rajasthan: open hills, villages and wild leopards.',
     [['How to connect them', 'From Jaipur, take a long drive, or take a train and then a taxi, or fly onward to Udaipur and drive to Bera. See [Jaipur to Jawai](blog/jaipur-to-jawai-distance-route-how-to-plan) for the practical details.'],
      ['A 9-day extension', '- Days 1–6: Delhi, Agra, Jaipur. || - Day 7: travel to Udaipur. || - Days 8–9: Jawai with two drives. || - Day 10: fly out from Udaipur or Jodhpur.'],
      ['Why it works', 'The pace slows right down after the cities, and you get the wildlife encounter many Golden Triangle trips lack. Add Ranakpur on the way for a heritage touch.']],
     [['Is Jawai too far from Jaipur for a short trip?', 'Roughly 450 km, so allow a full travel day or fly via Udaipur. It suits tours of eight days or more.'],
      ['Do I need to book safaris in advance?', 'Yes, especially in winter.'],
      ['Is Jawai suitable for first-time India travellers?', 'Yes. Private jeeps, a calm pace and English-speaking staff make it an easy introduction to wildlife.']], 'plan'],

    ['jawai-long-weekends-and-holidays-book-early-guide', 'Long Weekends and Holidays in Jawai: How Early to Book', 'Planning', '',
     'Jawai fills quickly on long weekends and festival weeks. Here is when to book and what to expect.',
     'Long Weekends and Holidays in Jawai: When and How to Book',
     'How to book Jawai for long weekends and holiday weeks: how far ahead to plan, crowd levels, safari slots and tips for a calmer trip.',
     'Jawai long weekend, Jawai holiday booking, Jawai crowded dates, book Jawai in advance, Jawai peak season dates',
     'Jawai is small, and good rooms and drives are limited. Holiday weeks fill early, so timing matters.',
     [['Which dates are busiest', 'Winter weekends, the Diwali period, Christmas to New Year and Republic Day weekends are the busiest. Summer holidays attract families who prefer cooler mornings.'],
      ['How early to book', 'Aim for four to six weeks ahead for peak weeks and two to three weeks for normal weekends. Request your safari slots at the same time as your room.'],
      ['Making a busy week calmer', '- Choose weekdays inside the holiday window. || - Prefer morning drives, which are often quieter. || - Add an extra night so you are not rushing. || - Keep one flexible drive in case weather or sightings change.']],
     [['Is Jawai crowded?', 'Much less than big national parks, but popular weekends still fill every room.'],
      ['Can I get a safari at short notice?', 'Sometimes, but it is never certain in peak weeks. Ask early.'],
      ['Are there price changes on holidays?', 'Rates can change with season and demand. Ask us for the rate on your dates.']], 'stay'],

    ['jawai-diwali-christmas-new-year-trip-what-to-expect', 'Diwali, Christmas and New Year in Jawai: What to Expect', 'Seasons', '',
     'What a festival-season trip to Jawai is like, from cold mornings to full jeeps, and how to plan it.',
     'Diwali, Christmas and New Year in Jawai: What to Expect',
     'A guide to festival-season trips to Jawai: Diwali, Christmas and New Year weather, crowds, safaris, food, celebrations and booking tips.',
     'Jawai Diwali trip, Jawai Christmas, Jawai New Year, Jawai festival season, Jawai winter holidays',
     'Festival weeks bring clear skies and cold mornings, and also the biggest demand. A little planning makes them magical.',
     [['Diwali', 'The weather is pleasant and the village is festive, with lamps and sweets. Safaris continue normally, though staff may have family commitments, so confirm timings. A quiet Diwali in the hills is a welcome change from city noise.'],
      ['Christmas and New Year', 'Expect cold dawns, full hotels and an excellent chance for birds and landscapes. Book your room and drives well ahead. A campfire evening at the hotel, if arranged, is a lovely way to ring in the new year.'],
      ['Practical tips', '- Pack warm layers for 6:00 AM drives. || - Reserve all drives with your room. || - Expect slower service on the busiest nights. || - Be patient with traffic on highways from Udaipur and Jodhpur.']],
     [['Is it very cold in Jawai at New Year?', 'Mornings are cold in the open jeep, often single digits to low teens Celsius, while afternoons are pleasant. Bring layers.'],
      ['Can we celebrate New Year at the hotel?', 'We can help with small private celebrations on request. See [private parties in Jawai](blog/private-parties-events-celebrations-in-jawai-bera).'],
      ['When should I book for New Year?', 'As early as you can, ideally a couple of months ahead.']], 'stay'],

    ['jawai-trip-booking-tips-changes-cancellations', 'Before You Pay: Booking Tips, Changes and Cancellations for a Jawai Trip', 'Planning', '',
     'A calm checklist for confirming a Jawai trip safely, including what to ask about changes and cancellation.',
     'Jawai Trip Booking Tips: Confirmation, Changes and Cancellation',
     'Booking tips for Jawai: how to confirm a safari and stay, what to ask about advance payment, changes and cancellations, and how to avoid scams.',
     'Jawai booking tips, Jawai cancellation policy, Jawai safari confirmation, avoid Jawai safari scam, Jawai booking changes',
     'A trip is easier when the booking is clear. These are the questions worth asking before you pay anyone.',
     [['Confirm in writing', 'Get your dates, room type, number of drives, inclusions and the final rate in a message or email. A WhatsApp message counts. Keep it saved. Our team confirms availability and rate personally and does not take online payment.'],
      ['Ask about advance and cancellation', '- How much advance, if any, and how is it paid? || - Can dates be changed, and is there a charge? || - What happens if rain or an emergency stops a drive? || - Who do I call on the morning of the drive?'],
      ['Beware of avoidable problems', 'Be careful with very cheap offers that need full payment upfront, vague inclusions or pressure to pay at once. Check the operator’s address, phone number and reviews. See our [policies](policies) for how we handle bookings and changes.']],
     [['Do you take online payment?', 'No. We confirm the booking by call or WhatsApp, and any advance is arranged directly with you.'],
      ['Can I change my dates after booking?', 'We try to move dates free of charge when we can, subject to availability. Tell us as early as possible.'],
      ['What if it rains on the day of the safari?', 'We will tell you honestly if conditions are poor and help reschedule where possible.']], 'plan'],

    ['jawai-trip-checklist-30-things-before-you-travel', 'Jawai Trip Checklist: 30 Things to Sort Before You Leave', 'Planning', '',
     'A printable-style checklist covering bookings, packing, money, health and the small things people forget.',
     'Jawai Trip Checklist: 30 Things to Do Before You Travel',
     'A complete Jawai travel checklist: bookings, documents, packing, money, health, photography and safari etiquette in one place.',
     'Jawai trip checklist, Jawai travel checklist, Jawai packing and planning, before you visit Jawai, Jawai travel preparation',
     'Use this list a week before you travel. It covers the things that make a Jawai trip run smoothly.',
     [['Bookings and documents', '- Room and safari slots confirmed in writing. || - Photo ID for every adult; passport for foreign guests. || - Train, flight or driver arranged, with pickup time shared. || - Hotel and emergency numbers saved.'],
      ['Packing and money', '- Neutral clothes, layers, hat, closed shoes. || - Binoculars, camera, spare battery, power bank. || - Sunscreen, repellent, personal medicines. || - Some cash for small purchases; mobile payments work in many places but not all. See [what to pack](blog/what-to-pack-for-jawai-safari).'],
      ['Health and comfort', '- Water bottle and snacks for drives. || - Motion-sickness tablets if needed. || - Tell the hotel about allergies and diets such as Jain food. || - Offline maps in case the signal drops.'],
      ['On the day', '- Be ready 10 minutes early. || - Stay seated and quiet. || - Follow your tracker. || - Take rubbish back with you. Read [safari rules and etiquette](blog/jawai-safari-rules-etiquette-responsible-travel).']],
     [['What is the one thing people forget?', 'Warm layers for the morning drive, even when the afternoon feels warm.'],
      ['Should I bring cash?', 'A little, for tips and village purchases. ATMs are in nearby towns, not always in the village itself.'],
      ['Is mobile signal reliable?', 'It can be patchy in the hills. Save the hotel’s number and download maps in advance.']], 'plan'],
    ];
}
